│                                                                    │
│ The core issue is that linkcheck incorrectly reports "Anchor not   │
│ found" when the server returns an HTTP error (like 404). The       │
│ current implementation seems to prioritize finding the anchor even │
│ when the server indicates a problem. The desired behavior, as      │
│ outlined in the issue, is to report the HTTP error itself,         │
│ mirroring the behavior when linkcheck_anchors is disabled.  The    │
│ fix involves modifying the linkcheck function to check the HTTP    │
│ status code and report it if it’s an error, rather than continuing │
│ to search for an anchor.                                           │
